<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Megüjin Seultü</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 1196</span> · <a href="/centuries/12th-century">12th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Megüjin Seultü was a chief of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tatars">Tatars</a> of eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mongolia">Mongolia</a>. In 1196 the Jin dynasty, which had turned against its former Tatar allies, sent an army against him, joined by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/genghis-khan">Temüjin</a>, the future Genghis Khan, and the Keraite ruler <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ong-khan">Toghrul</a>. He was defeated and killed at the Ulz river, and the Jin rewarded Temüjin with a title.</p></div>
